{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Joseph said to his brothers...and Joseph swore, etc.</b> It is surprising: why did he say twice פקד יפקוד? It should have written: 'I am dying, and swear to me that when Elohim surely visits you, you shall bring up my bones, etc.' And one may answer that this is what it says: Jacob our father said, ״Elohim will surely visit you and bring you up,״ and ״you shall bring up my bones״ — and therefore: ״when Elohim surely visits, etc.״ And the verse states: ״אנכי אעשה כדבריך״ — this is what Derish Sadera says." "<b>Elohim will surely visit.</b> This means: by the numerical value of פקוד״ — the Holy One, blessed be He, will deduct from your exile. He prophesied about them that they would not be in Egypt except רד״ו [210] years. Thus you learn that the Holy One, blessed be He, deducted from the servitude a number of years equal to the numerical value of פקוד יפקד אלהים. And the word יפקוד is interpreted as in ״ולא נפקד ממנו איש״. However, it is difficult for me, for I found פקד defective [missing] vav, and it appears that if we say יש אם למקרא, it works out."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {1 "פקוד spelled without vav yields 186, not 210; with vav yields 192. The arithmetic does not produce רד״ו (210) under standard calculation; the difficulty is left as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:41.717564971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}